      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-sample/q6",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show on an Argand diagram the locus of points given by the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> satisfying<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left|z-4-3\\mathrm i\\right|=5\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li></ol><p>Taking the initial line as the positive real axis with the pole at the origin and given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\in[\\alpha,\\,\\alpha+\\pi]\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=-\\arctan\\left(\\dfrac43\\right)\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\" start=\"2\"><li>show that this locus of points can be represented by the polar curve with equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=8\\cos\\theta+6\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>The set of points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\left\\{z:0\\leqslant\\arg z\\leqslant\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right\\}\\cap\\left\\{z:\\left|z-4-3\\mathrm i\\right|\\leqslant5\\right\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show, by shading on your Argand diagram, the set of points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</li><li>Find the <strong>exact</strong> area of the region defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, giving your answer in simplest form.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li></ol>",
